quran[32]{c,v,t}:
  86,1,By the (endless expanse and infinite space of) heaven and the Nightly (discernable) Visitant.
  86,2,And what do you know what the Nightly (discernable) Visitant is?
  86,3,"(It implies) every heavenly body (be it a star, a planet, or any of the heavenly spheres) which shines and brightens (the space).*"
  86,4,There is no human soul but with a protector (appointed) over it.
  86,5,So man should ponder (and find out) from what substance he has been created.
  86,6,"He has been created from the ejaculated fluid (i.e., virile and motile sperm)."
  86,7,That proceeds from the middle of the sacrum (and pelvic girdle) and is ejected.
  86,8,"Indeed, He has the power to bring it (life) back,"
  86,9,The Day when all secrets will be disclosed.
  86,10,Then man will have neither any strength (himself) nor any helper.
  86,11,"By the heavenly universe which will regress to its primitive state,"
  86,12,"And by the earth which will split asunder (and change into dust particles),"
  86,13,"This is indeed a decisive (i.e., absolute) commandment."
  86,14,And it is no joke!
  86,15,"Indeed, they (the disbelievers) are hatching plots."
  86,16,And I am designing My own strategy.
  86,17,"So give the disbelievers a respite (for a while, not much); let them relax a little (more)."
  87,1,"Glorify the Name of your Lord, the Most High,"
  87,2,"He Who has created (everything in the universe) and then (fulfilling all requisites) equipoised it to its exact proportion,"
  87,3,"And He Who has determined law, and guided (it to its) way (of sustaining and functioning according to its respective system),"
  87,4,"And He Who has brought forth green pasture (from the earth),"
  87,5,And then made it blackened stubble.
  87,6,"(O Esteemed Beloved!) We shall teach you (in a way) that nothing will you (ever) forget,"
  87,7,"Except what Allah wills. Indeed, He knows all, the manifest as well as the hidden (i.e., open to human perception as well as veiled from it, and the audible and the inaudible)."
  87,8,And We shall (also) facilitate you (to put into practice this) easy (law).
  87,9,"So keep admonishing, provided admonition benefits (the listeners)."
  87,10,But only he who fears (Allah) will accept the admonition.
  87,11,"And the wretched one will avoid and evade it,"
  87,12,He who will enter the greatest Fire (on the Day of Judgment).
  87,13,Then he will neither die nor live in it.
  87,14,"Indeed, only he who is purified (from the afflictions of his ill-commanding self and pollution of sins) will triumph,"
  87,15,And the one who remembers the Name of his Lord and offers Prayers (regularly and abundantly).
